# Listed again, after the catch-all, because GitHub applies the last matching
# rule and because this path is the one that matters. A required status check
# is matched by its name, so a pull request with write access can replace a
# caller with a stub emitting that name and exiting zero. The reusable cannot
# prevent it: the caller lives in the repository the pull request edits, and
# GitHub runs the pull request's version.
#
# The mitigation is ruleset-side: require review from Code Owners on this path,
# so a pull request neutralizing a caller cannot merge without its owner seeing
# the diff. It needs this file to exist, which is why it is here already.
.github/workflows/      @Jaro-c
